<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix for Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<figure id="A1.F1.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:120.8pt;">
<div id="A1.F1.fig1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:224.3pt;"><img src="2510.01387v1/figures/br_region_2.png" id="A1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:303/242;" width="303" height="242" alt="Refer to caption">
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span> A single-follower best-response region with <math id="A1.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math> types and two follower actions and three leader actions – <math id="A1.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=2,L=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=2,L=3</annotation></semantics></math>. The triangle represents the probability simplex <math id="A1.F1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>. The three hyperplanes defined by <math id="A1.F1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.F1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}(1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{3}(1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{3}(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> partition the simplex into best-response regions. For example, in region <math id="A1.F1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(w_{0,1,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(w_{0,1,1})</annotation></semantics></math>, the follower best-responds with action <math id="A1.F1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for type <math id="A1.F1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and action <math id="A1.F1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> for types <math id="A1.F1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> followers each with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> type and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> actions. Each follower has <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\binom{A}{2}\leq KA^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\binom{A}{2}\leq KA^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> advantage vectors, where each advantage vector <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta,a,a^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta,a,a^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a hyperplane in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> that separates the leader’s mixed strategy space <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\mathcal{L})\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\mathcal{L})\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> into two halfspaces. In total, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> followers have <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nKA^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nKA^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> hyperplanes. Those hyperplanes divide <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> into at most <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((nKA^{2})^{L})=\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((nKA^{2})^{L})=\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})</annotation></semantics></math> regions (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Halperin and Sharir [2017]</a></cite>).
Each non-empty best response region is one of such regions, so the total number is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ALGORITHM 4</span> </span>Best-Response Region Enumeration</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
Let <math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{isFeasible}(x,i,\theta,a)=\mathds{1}\left[\forall a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A},~\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}}x(\ell)\big(v_{i}(\ell,a,\theta)-v_{i}(\ell,a^{\prime},\theta)\big)\geq 0\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>isFeasible</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">,</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{isFeasible}(x,i,\theta,a)=\mathds{1}\left[\forall a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A},~\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{L}}x(\ell)\big(v_{i}(\ell,a,\theta)-v_{i}(\ell,a^{\prime},\theta)\big)\geq 0\right]</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">Let <math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{findFeasible}(W)=\big\{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})\,|\,\forall i\in[n],\theta\in\Theta,\text{isFeasible}(x,i,\theta,W[i,\theta])=1\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>findFeasible</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>isFeasible</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{findFeasible}(W)=\big\{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})\,|\,\forall i\in[n],\theta\in\Theta,\text{isFeasible}(x,i,\theta,W[i,\theta])=1\big\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">Choose a random strategy <math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{init}\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{init}\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><span id="algorithm4.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text">isFeasible</span><math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{init},i,\theta,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{init},i,\theta,a)</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{init}[i,\theta]=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{init}[i,\theta]=a</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">Let <math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="queue=[W_{init}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">queue=[W_{init}]</annotation></semantics></math>,  mark <math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{init}</annotation></semantics></math> as <em id="algorithm4.4.8.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">visited</em> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="queue\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">queue\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=queue.pop()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=queue.pop()</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.12.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq W[i,\theta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq W[i,\theta]</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Let <math id="algorithm4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}=W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}=W</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Let <math id="algorithm4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}[i,\theta]=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}[i,\theta]=a</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.15.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{findFeasible}(W)\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">findFeasible</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{findFeasible}(W)\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is not visited</em> <span id="algorithm4.4.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="queue.append(W^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">queue.append(W^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>,  mark <math id="algorithm4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as <em id="algorithm4.4.16.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">visited</em>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.17" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We construct a graph <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the elements <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, each representing a best-response region. An edge exists between two vertices <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> differ in exactly one entry. Traversing an edge corresponds to moving between adjacent best-response regions by crossing a hyperplane boundary.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that this graph is connected.
Since each vertex <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a best-response region defined by the inequalities in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and the leader’s strategy space is the <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional probability simplex, the union of non-empty best response regions forms a partition of the strategy space. Because these regions are convex polytopes sharing boundaries, the adjacent structure defined by differing in one entry corresponds to crossing a shared facet. Starting from any non-empty region, we can traverse to any other by crossing shared facets through adjacent regions, so the graph is connected.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, to enumerate all non-empty best-response regions, we can perform a graph search (e.g., breadth-first search or depth-first search) starting from any initial vertex <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> to traverse all vertices in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|W|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|W|)</annotation></semantics></math> steps, which is <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Specifically, at each vertex <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, we examine all its adjacent <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nKA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nKA</annotation></semantics></math> vertices. For each adjacent vertex <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we determine whether <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(W^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(W^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-empty region by solving a feasibility linear program defined by the constraints in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), which runs in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(n,K,A,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(n,K,A,L)</annotation></semantics></math> time. Then, the total running time is <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(n^{L},K^{L},A^{L},L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(n^{L},K^{L},A^{L},L)</annotation></semantics></math>. We present the algorithm formally in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm4" title="In A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Appendix for Section ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix for Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following definitions will be used in the proofs for this section:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Total variation distance)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For two discrete distributions <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> over support <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the total variation is half the <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between the two distributions:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\mathcal{D},\hat{\mathcal{D}})=\frac{1}{2}||\mathcal{D}-\hat{\mathcal{D}}||_{1}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\theta\in\Theta}|\mathcal{D}(\theta)-\hat{\mathcal{D}}(\theta)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\mathcal{D},\hat{\mathcal{D}})=\frac{1}{2}||\mathcal{D}-\hat{\mathcal{D}}||_{1}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\theta\in\Theta}|\mathcal{D}(\theta)-\hat{\mathcal{D}}(\theta)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hellinger distance)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For two discrete distributions <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> over support <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the Hellinger distance is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathcal{D},\hat{\mathcal{D}})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\|\sqrt{\mathcal{D}}-\sqrt{\hat{\mathcal{D}}}\|_{2}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{\theta\in\Theta}\big(\mathcal{D}(\theta)-\hat{\mathcal{D}}(\theta)\big)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathcal{D},\hat{\mathcal{D}})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\|\sqrt{\mathcal{D}}-\sqrt{\hat{\mathcal{D}}}\|_{2}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{\theta\in\Theta}\big(\mathcal{D}(\theta)-\hat{\mathcal{D}}(\theta)\big)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ General Type Distributions: ‣ 4.1 Learning Algorithms and Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We rely on several key insights about the <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pseudo-dimension</em> of a family of functions, defined below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition 10.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mohri et al. [2012]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a family of functions from input space <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to real numbers <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A set of inputs </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z_{1},\ldots,z_{m}\}\subseteq\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z_{1},\ldots,z_{m}\}\subseteq\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph">shattered</em><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if there exists thresholds </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},\ldots,t_{m}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},\ldots,t_{m}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for any sign vector </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})\in\{-1,+1\}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})\in\{-1,+1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there exists a function </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sign}(g(x_{i})-t_{i})=\sigma_{i}\text{ for all }i=1,...m." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">sign</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sign}(g(x_{i})-t_{i})=\sigma_{i}\text{ for all }i=1,...m.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The size of the largest set of inputs that can be shattered by </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is called the </span><em id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph">pseudo-dimension</em><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a family of functions with a finite pseudo-dimension, and samples <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{1},\ldots,z^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{1},\ldots,z^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from a distribution on the input space <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, the empirical mean of any function in the family will, with high probability, be close to the true mean. Formally:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(e.g., Theorem 10.6 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mohri et al. [2012]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a family of functions from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with pseudo-dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})=d</annotation></semantics></math>. For any distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> over the random draw of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{1},\ldots,z^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{1},\ldots,z^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim F}[g(z)]-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}g(z^{i})\,\Big|~\leq~\sqrt{\frac{2d\log 3N}{N}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta}}{2N}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.330em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim F}[g(z)]-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}g(z^{i})\,\Big|~\leq~\sqrt{\frac{2d\log 3N}{N}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta}}{2N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the family of linear functions over <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{g_{x}:z\to\langle x,z\rangle\mid x\in\mathbb{R}^{L}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{g_{x}:z\to\langle x,z\rangle\mid x\in\mathbb{R}^{L}\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
It is known that the pseudo-dimension of this family is <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(e.g., Theorem 10.4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mohri et al. [2012]</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The family of linear functions <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{g_{x}:z\to\langle x,z\rangle\mid x\in\mathbb{R}^{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{g_{x}:z\to\langle x,z\rangle\mid x\in\mathbb{R}^{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> has pseudo-dimension <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ General Type Distributions: ‣ 4.1 Learning Algorithms and Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now have the tools to prove Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ General Type Distributions: ‣ 4.1 Learning Algorithms and Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. For any non-empty best-response region defined by <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, …, <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{t}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{t}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d samples. For each sample <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can directly compute</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{i}}=\Big(u(1,W(\bm{\theta}^{i})),...,u(L,W(\bm{\theta}^{i}))\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{i}}=\Big(u(1,W(\bm{\theta}^{i})),...,u(L,W(\bm{\theta}^{i}))\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any leader strategy <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in R(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in R(W)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.2 Multiple Followers ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>,
the leader’s expected utility by using strategy <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[\langle x,z_{W,\bm{\theta}}\rangle]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[\langle x,z_{W,\bm{\theta}}\rangle]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the expectation of the linear function <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})=\langle x,z_{W,\bm{\theta}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})=\langle x,z_{W,\bm{\theta}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (e.g., Theorem 10.6 in [ ] ). ‣ B.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Appendix for Section ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma B.1 (e.g., Theorem 10.4 in [ ] ). ‣ B.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Appendix for Section ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\forall x\in R(W),~\Big|\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})]-\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{i}})\Big|\leq\sqrt{\frac{2L\log 3t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta^{\prime}}}{2t}}~\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\forall x\in R(W),~\Big|\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})]-\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{i}})\Big|\leq\sqrt{\frac{2L\log 3t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta^{\prime}}}{2t}}~\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[g_{x}(z_{W,\bm{\theta}})]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{U}^{t}(x)=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}g(z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}^{t}(x)=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{t}g(z_{W,\bm{\theta}^{t}})</annotation></semantics></math>. So,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\forall x\in R(W),~\Big|U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)-\hat{U}^{t}(x)\Big|\leq\sqrt{\frac{2L\log 3t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta^{\prime}}}{2t}}~\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.330em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\forall x\in R(W),~\Big|U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)-\hat{U}^{t}(x)\Big|\leq\sqrt{\frac{2L\log 3t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{1}{\delta^{\prime}}}{2t}}~\right]\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\frac{\delta}{|\mathcal{W}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\frac{\delta}{|\mathcal{W}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the union bound, with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the following bound holds simultaneously for all <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in R(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in R(W)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)-\hat{U}^{t}(x)\Big|\,\leq\,\sqrt{\frac{2L\log(3t)}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{|\mathcal{W}|}{\delta}}{2t}}\,=\,\mathcal{O}\bigg(\sqrt{\frac{L\log t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{L\log(nKA)+\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}{t}}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|U_{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}(x)-\hat{U}^{t}(x)\Big|\,\leq\,\sqrt{\frac{2L\log(3t)}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log\frac{|\mathcal{W}|}{\delta}}{2t}}\,=\,\mathcal{O}\bigg(\sqrt{\frac{L\log t}{t}}+\sqrt{\frac{L\log(nKA)+\log(\frac{1}{\delta})}{t}}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the fact <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{W}|=O(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{W}|=O(n^{L}K^{L}A^{2L})</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.3 Enumerating Best-Response Regions and Computing the Offline Optimal ‣ 3 Best Response Regions: A Geometric Perspective ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ General Type Distributions: ‣ 4.1 Learning Algorithms and Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{K^{n}T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\sqrt{K^{n}T})</annotation></semantics></math> Regret:</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a Bayesian Stackelberg game with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> followers each with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> types, with joint type distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(x,\bm{\mathcal{D}})=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[u(x,{\bm{\mathrm{br}}}(\bm{\theta},x))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(x,\bm{\mathcal{D}})=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{\theta}\sim\bm{\mathcal{D}}}[u(x,{\bm{\mathrm{br}}}(\bm{\theta},x))]</annotation></semantics></math> be the expected utility of the leader playing mixed strategy <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> when the type distribution is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}=\arg\max_{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})}U(x,\bm{\mathcal{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}=\arg\max_{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})}U(x,\bm{\mathcal{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal strategy for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. At each round <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In General Type Distributions: ‣ 4.1 Learning Algorithms and Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Type Feedback ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> chooses the optimal strategy <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{t}=\argmax_{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})}U(x,\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{t}=\argmax_{x\in\Delta(\mathcal{L})}U(x,\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> for the empirical distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> samples. The total expected regret is equal to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Reg}(T)]=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}\Big[\underbrace{U(x^{*},\bm{\mathcal{D}})-U(x^{t},\bm{\mathcal{D}})}_{\text{single-round regret $r(t)$}}\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Reg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>single-round regret </mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Reg}(T)]=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}\Big[\underbrace{U(x^{*},\bm{\mathcal{D}})-U(x^{t},\bm{\mathcal{D}})}_{\text{single-round regret $r(t)$}}\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We upper bound the single-round regret <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> by the total variation distance (Definition <a href="#A2.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition B.1 (Total variation distance). ‣ Appendix B Appendix for Section ‣ Learning to Play Multi-Follower Bayesian Stackelberg Games" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) between <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmclaim1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmclaim1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmclaim1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmclaim1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmclaim1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.Thmclaim1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)=U(x^{*},\bm{\mathcal{D}})-U(x^{t},\bm{\mathcal{D}})\leq 4\delta(\bm{\mathcal{D}},\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓓</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)=U(x^{*},\bm{\mathcal{D}})-U(x^{t},\bm{\mathcal{D}})\leq 4\delta(\bm{\mathcal{D}},\hat{\bm{\mathcal{D}}}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmclaim1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
